# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Nebutra-instance ops vs Sailor-product boundary
# Nebutra-Sailor is one Nebutra deployment AND the Sailor template. Anything
# true only for Nebutra's own instance — its Fly org, its DNS zone, its Vercel
# team, its ECS host, its bills — lives in one of three declared homes and
# never ships in the mirror (TEMPLATE.md "Instance vs product"):
#   ops/                        instance-only config (ops/nebutra/README.md)
#   docs/ops/nebutra/           instance runbooks (bills, cutovers, hosts)
#   tests/architecture/nebutra/ tests that assert Nebutra-instance facts
# Workflows and Fly manifests have no directory split, so they are listed.
# The rule: a workflow ships in the template only when it carries no Nebutra
# instance literal (nebutra.com host, nebutra-* Fly/Worker app, ECS IP,
# Vercel team id). Guard: tests/architecture/template-boundary.test.ts builds
# the template and scans the output; scripts/template-check.ts checks the
# rules statically. `/ops/` is anchored on purpose — a bare `ops/` would also
# match packages/ops/ and infra/ops/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/ops/
docs/ops/nebutra/
tests/architecture/nebutra/
